    "created_at": "2017-04-27T09:34:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-27T09:34:25Z",
    "body": "It wouldn't really result in less parser code though. In Chromium this would be basically changing [this line](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/page/WindowFeatures.cpp?q=windowfeatures+package:%5Echromium$&l=170) from setting to true to instead setting to `value`. So I think the main benefit is consistency, and allowing developers to do things like:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst features = `noopener=${noopener_enabled},toolbar=${toolbar_enabled}`;\r\n```\r\ninstead of something more convoluted like:\r\n```js\r\nconst noopener = noopener_enabled ? \"noopener,\" : \"\";\r\nconst features = `${noopener}toolbar=${toolbar_enabled}`;\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/297664333/reactions",
